---
import PolicyLayout from '../layouts/PolicyLayout.astro';
---

<PolicyLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | Miami Debt Help"
  description="Miami Debt Help privacy policy — what information we collect, how it's used, and what we never do with it."
  lang="en"
  altLangPath="/es/privacy/"
  breadcrumbLabel="Privacy Policy"
  h1="Privacy Policy"
  lastUpdated="Last updated: August 20, 2026"
>
  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <p>
    Miami Debt Help does not require an account or login to use the site. We collect two kinds
    of information:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Analytics data.</strong> Standard web analytics (page views, general location at
      the city/region level, device and browser type, referring site) collected automatically
      through Google Analytics, using cookies. This is aggregate usage data — it's not tied to
      your name or used to identify you individually.</li>
    <li><strong>Information you submit directly.</strong> If you use the <a href="/submit-a-listing/">
      listing</a> or <a href="/report-an-error/">error report</a> forms, or the anonymous
      question box on the homepage, we collect what you type into that form. The question box is
      anonymous by design and doesn't ask for contact information; the other forms ask for an
      email only when you want a response.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How we use it</h2>
  <p>
    Analytics data shapes what content we prioritize — for example, noticing that a lot of
    people are asking about wage garnishment tells us that's worth a dedicated guide. Information
    submitted through a form is used to act on that specific submission: reviewing a listing
    request, correcting a reported error, or following up if you asked us to.
  </p>

  <h2>What we don't do</h2>
  <p>
    We do not sell personal information to third parties, and we never sell a visitor's contact
    information to multiple buyers or use it for warm transfers, robocalls, or SMS marketing —
    see <a href="/how-we-make-money/">How We Make Money</a> for the fuller set of hard lines this
    site operates under.
  </p>

  <h2>Cookies</h2>
  <p>
    This site uses cookies through Google Analytics to measure usage. You can block or delete
    cookies through your browser settings; the site will still function, though usage
    measurement won't.
  </p>

  <h2>Third-party services</h2>
  <p>
    Google Analytics processes the usage data described above under its own privacy terms. As
    form submissions get connected to a processing service, that service and its role will be
    named here before it goes live.
  </p>

  <h2>Children's privacy</h2>
  <p>This site is not directed at children under 13 and does not knowingly collect information from them.</p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    If this policy changes in a way that matters, the "last updated" date above will change and,
    for a significant change, we'll note what changed rather than silently editing it.
  </p>

  <h2>Questions</h2>
  <p>See <a href="/contact/">Contact</a>.</p>
</PolicyLayout>
